  "title": "D-reviewhint finish 2 (T-1585 lineage): the bounding test measures the diff section, not the whole packet",
  "spec": "Goal T-1403, plan label D-reviewhint-finish2. Finishes T-1638 (and through it T-1585). Fresh task: the Planner created your branch task/THIS-TASK at 96e92fe (head of task/T-1638: the whole D-reviewhint change plus T-1638's test fixes). Keep everything already committed; touch only tests/test_spawn.py; do not change orchestrator/spawn.py.\n\nGate failure on 96e92fe (full suite): FAIL tests/test_spawn.py Render.test_review_packet_single_bounding_pass_no_nested_truncation: assertLessEqual(len(text), 8200) got 11375. The test builds a packet with a 1500-char acceptance, a 1500-char scope entry and 1500-char failure text, and a ~34k-char diff, with [limits].review_diff_chars 8000. The T-1585 spec deliberately changed the budget: the diff section is capped at review_diff_chars and the other sections are NOT subtracted, so the whole packet may exceed the cap. The assertion on the whole packet is wrong; the code is right.\n\nChange the test only: instead of len(text) <= 8200, extract the diff section of the packet (the text after the diff section heading up to the next '## ' heading or the end; read review_packet to find the exact heading) and assert its length is at most 8000 plus the truncation marker and expand-hint lines (allow 8000 + 600); also assert the diff section is shorter than the raw diff (it was cut) and that len(text) > 8200 is allowed (no whole-packet assertion). Keep the two existing assertions on 'expand with:' (exactly one occurrence, and the exact hint text). No other test changes.\n\nVerify: commit first. Then, in the foreground, run tests/test_spawn.py, then the whole tests directory once with the command .claude/hooks/tests-green.sh uses; report failures only and state that the full run happened and its result. Never background a command.",
  "inputs": [
    "T-1638",
    "T-1585"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_spawn.py::test_review_packet_hint_names_base_range_and_branch: passes: for a task whose worktree has one commit beyond goal/<parent>, review_packet's expand hint is exactly the scoped_diff command with the goal base (`git -C <wt> diff -U3 goal/<parent>...HEAD -- <scope>`), the packet's base line shows the merge-base short sha (not HEAD), and the packet names the branch under review (task['branch'] when set, else task/<id>) with the HEAD short sha; with no goal branch the hint and base use origin/main",
    "tests/test_spawn.py::test_review_packet_diff_budget_honours_review_diff_chars: passes: with [limits].review_diff_chars 20000 and a scoped diff of 15000 chars, the packet contains the whole diff and no 'more lines' marker; with review_diff_chars 3000 the diff section is cut with the marker and the hint from the first test; the packet never cuts the diff at 8000 when the configured value is larger",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh wt/THIS-TASK exits 0"
